# python3, toolchain llvm
### --with-lto compiles every object with -flto=thin, and CPython asks for fat objects only from gcc
### (-flto -fuse-linker-plugin -ffat-lto-objects). The config directory of the installation gets
### libpython<ver>.a and python.o whatever --disable-static says, and with clang they would hold
### bytecode and nothing else, which names the build host: build stops on them. Fat objects keep their
### machine code, the only part strip_lto_objects leaves in the package
PKG_CFLAGS+=" -ffat-lto-objects"
